Gym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.
Please upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.
Users of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.
See the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.
E3 smoke test completed successfully. All 5 alpha values ran and the JSON with 5 entries was saved correctly.

The Pareto results with only 5 episodes show identical n_operators=10 across all alphas — this is expected since SB3-PPO runs 2048 timesteps regardless of the episode count setting, and the alpha complexity penalty doesn't yet differentiate enough with so few training steps. With full 300-episode runs, lower alpha values would apply greater complexity pressure during training, guiding the agent toward shorter circuits.

All three experiment runners (E1, E2, E3) are confirmed working correctly.
All user stories in `prd.json` have `passes: true` and `progress.txt` confirms all 6 stories (US-009 through US-014) are complete.

